<section class="page-head">
  <p class="kicker">Limb V</p>
  <h1>Neurobiology</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">Three pounds of electrified fat that models a universe. Everything this order studies —
  the vision, the grove, the star, the god — arrives through it, which makes the organ the one instrument we
  cannot afford to be romantic about.</p>
</section>

<!-- ============================== THE PREMISE ============================= -->
<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--first">
    <p class="kicker">Begin Here</p>
    <h2>The Instrument Problem</h2>
    <p class="lede">An astronomer who refused to learn the optics of their telescope would be laughed out of the
    observatory. Yet most people pursuing the inner life never learn the first thing about the apparatus
    producing it.</p>

    <p>Every experience this order takes seriously — the sense of presence in a wood at dusk, the geometry
    behind closed eyes, the conviction of contact, the dissolution of self at the peak of a meditation — is
    delivered by a biological system with known tissue, known chemistry and known failure modes. That is not a
    debunking. It is the opposite: it is the only route to telling a genuine signal from an artefact of the
    receiver.</p>

    <p>So the rule for this limb is severe. <strong>Describing the mechanism of an experience says nothing
    whatsoever about whether its content is true.</strong> Finding the serotonin receptor involved in a vision
    no more disproves the vision than finding the rods and cones disproves the Moon. But it does mean that
    "it felt utterly real" is a statement about the apparatus, not about reality — and the apparatus is
    demonstrably capable of manufacturing total conviction out of nothing at all.</p>

    <p class="muted small">Grading throughout: <span class="sci">◆ established science</span> ·
    <span class="hist">◆ scholarship and history</span> · <span class="spec">◆ speculative and contested</span> ·
    <span class="myth">◆ myth, tradition and primary esoteric text</span>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<!-- ============================== THE PLATES ============================== -->
<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">Seven Plates</p>
    <h2>The Machinery, Plate by Plate</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">From one cell to the whole predictive apparatus, and then out to the edge where the
    evidence thins.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid two">

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate I <span class="sci">◆</span></p>
      <h3>The Cell That Decides</h3>
      <p>A neuron holds roughly −70 millivolts across its membrane, maintained by pumps burning a fifth of your
      body's entire energy budget. Inputs arrive at thousands of synapses; if the summed voltage crosses about
      −55 mV the cell fires an all-or-nothing spike, propagating at up to 120 metres per second.</p>
      <p>Roughly 86 billion of them, with an equivalent number of glia doing work we badly underestimated for a
      century. The spike itself carries no meaning. Meaning lives in <em>which</em> cells fire, <em>when</em>,
      and what the pattern has been wired to predict.</p>
      <p class="muted small">Hodgkin &amp; Huxley worked out the ionic mechanism on a squid giant axon and took
      the 1963 Nobel for it. Azevedo <em>et al.</em> (2009) replaced the folkloric "100 billion" with an
      actual count.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate II <span class="sci">◆</span></p>
      <h3>Plasticity, or Why Practice Works</h3>
      <p>Synapses that are repeatedly active together strengthen; those that are not, weaken and are pruned.
      Long-term potentiation is measurable in a slice of hippocampus within minutes, and involves physical
      trafficking of receptors into the membrane.</p>
      <p>This is the honest biological core of every contemplative tradition's insistence on daily practice.
      You are not accumulating merit. You are rewiring a physical organ by repetition, in the same way and by
      the same mechanism as learning an instrument — and like an instrument, it degrades when abandoned.</p>
      <p class="muted small">Note what this does <em>not</em> license: "neuroplasticity" is not a permission
      slip for any claim you like. Adult brains change in specific, bounded, slow ways.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate III <span class="sci">◆</span></p>
      <h3>Rhythm and the Binding of a Moment</h3>
      <p>Populations of neurons oscillate together — delta through theta, alpha, beta and gamma. Alpha
      (≈8–12 Hz) rises when the eyes close; theta (≈4–8 Hz) dominates hippocampal navigation and deep
      absorption; gamma (≈30–100 Hz) accompanies tightly bound perception.</p>
      <p>Rhythm appears to be how a brain decides what belongs with what: cells firing in phase are treated as
      reporting on the same thing. It is also the mechanism by which drumming, chant and flicker genuinely
      alter state — a periodic drive can pull an oscillator towards its own tempo.</p>
      <p class="muted small">The entrainment effect is real and well documented for photic drive. The popular
      claim that specific frequencies unlock specific spiritual states is <span class="spec">◆ not</span>.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate IV <span class="sci">◆</span></p>
      <h3>The Brain as a Prediction Engine</h3>
      <p>The dominant modern account inverts the naive picture. The brain is not primarily receiving the world;
      it is generating a model of the world and sending it <em>downwards</em>, while the senses return only the
      error — the part the model got wrong. Perception is a controlled hallucination that the data keeps
      correcting.</p>
      <p>It explains an enormous amount: why expectation changes what you see, why pain is modulated by belief,
      why a face appears in bark, why the first night in a strange house is full of intruders. The prior is
      doing most of the work, always, in everyone.</p>
      <p class="muted small">Helmholtz's 1867 "unconscious inference", formalised by Friston, Clark and Hohwy.
      Dominant and productive — but a framework, not a settled fact.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate V <span class="sci">◆</span></p>
      <h3>The Default Mode Network</h3>
      <p>When a person stops doing a task, a specific set of midline structures — medial prefrontal cortex,
      posterior cingulate, precuneus, angular gyrus — becomes <em>more</em> active. This network handles
      autobiography, mental time travel, modelling other minds, and the running narrative of being a self.</p>
      <p>It is the closest thing neuroscience has to a physical correlate of the ego in the technical sense:
      not arrogance, but the continuous construction of a protagonist. Its activity is reduced in experienced
      meditators, and strongly disrupted by classic psychedelics.</p>
      <p class="muted small">Raichle (2001) named it. Brewer <em>et al.</em> (2011) found the meditation effect;
      Carhart-Harris <em>et al.</em> (2012) the psilocybin one.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate VI <span class="sci">◆</span></p>
      <h3>The 5-HT2A Key</h3>
      <p>Psilocybin, LSD, mescaline and DMT differ chemically but converge on one action: agonism at the
      serotonin 5-HT2A receptor, densely expressed on layer-5 pyramidal cells of the cortex. Block that
      receptor with ketanserin and the experience simply does not occur.</p>
      <p>Downstream, the cortex becomes less hierarchically constrained. Regions that normally do not talk begin
      to; the prior loosens its grip on the error signal. On the predictive account above, that is precisely
      what a vision <em>is</em> — a model running with the brakes off.</p>
      <p>The clinical findings for depression and end-of-life distress are genuinely promising and genuinely
      preliminary: small samples, near-impossible blinding, enormous expectancy effects.</p>
      <p class="muted small">Nothing on this page is medical advice. These are powerful, legally controlled
      compounds with real psychiatric risk, particularly where psychosis runs in a family.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <p class="tag">Plate VII <span class="sci">◆</span></p>
      <h3>Form Constants: Why the Geometry</h3>
      <p>People across every culture and every method — peyote, migraine, flicker, pressure on the eyeball,
      sensory deprivation, near-death — report the same four classes of figure: lattices and honeycombs,
      cobwebs, tunnels and funnels, spirals.</p>
      <p>There is a strong explanation. The retina maps onto primary visual cortex in an approximately
      logarithmic-polar fashion. Under that mapping, simple stripes of spontaneous activity rolling across flat
      cortex are <em>seen</em> as concentric rings, radiating spokes and logarithmic spirals. The geometry of
      the vision is the geometry of the cortical sheet, read through a known distortion.</p>
      <p class="muted small">Klüver catalogued the constants in 1926; Ermentrout &amp; Cowan modelled them in
      1979; Bressloff <em>et al.</em> (2001) tied them to cortical symmetry. See
      <a href="/sacred-geometry/">Limb III</a> — this is where the two limbs meet, and it is the most honest
      thing we can say about why sacred art looks the way it does.</p>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<!-- ============================== THE LEDGER ============================== -->
<section class="wrap">
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h2>What Survives Scrutiny</h2>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> Meditation measurably alters attention networks and reduces default mode activity in long-term practitioners.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> Classic psychedelics act at 5-HT2A and reliably disrupt hierarchical cortical processing.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> Form constants are explained by the retinocortical map — a real bridge from vision to geometry.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> Photic and auditory rhythm can entrain cortical oscillations.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> The gut hosts ~500 million neurons and its microbiome influences mood and behaviour in animal models.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> Experience physically rewires tissue: plasticity is structural, not metaphorical.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> Sleep clears metabolic waste from neural tissue; chronic deprivation damages cognition severely.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> Psychedelic-assisted therapy shows real promise in small trials for treatment-resistant depression.</li>
        <li><span class="sci">◆</span> Interoception — the sense of the body's internal state — is a major input to emotion, not a sideshow.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h2>What Does Not</h2>
      <ul class="biblio">
        <li><span class="myth">◆</span> <strong>"You use 10% of your brain."</strong> Fabricated. Imaging shows essentially all of it active across a day; damage anywhere costs you something.</li>
        <li><span class="myth">◆</span> <strong>Left-brain / right-brain personalities.</strong> Lateralisation of specific functions is real; "creative" versus "logical" people is not.</li>
        <li><span class="myth">◆</span> <strong>The pineal gland as the third eye secreting DMT.</strong> It makes melatonin. Trace DMT has been found in rodent pineal tissue at concentrations nowhere near psychoactive.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">◆</span> <strong>Binaural beats as a state technology.</strong> Pleasant, mildly relaxing, repeatedly fails to deliver the advertised specific states.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">◆</span> <strong>Quantum consciousness in microtubules.</strong> Not impossible, but the decoherence objection at body temperature remains unanswered after thirty years.</li>
        <li><span class="spec">◆</span> <strong>"Rewire your brain in 21 days."</strong> Durable structural change takes months of consistent practice, and the number is marketing.</li>
        <li><span class="myth">◆</span> <strong>Learning styles.</strong> Tested repeatedly, never found. Teach to the material, not the self-report.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted small mt-1">Each of these is believed sincerely by people we like. That is exactly why
      they are listed.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<!-- ============================ THE HARD PROBLEM ========================== -->
<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">The Open Wound</p>
    <h2>Nobody Knows Why Any of It Is Lit</h2>
    <p class="lede">Everything above describes function. None of it explains experience.</p>
    <p>We can say in detail how light at 700 nanometres is transduced, relayed, and categorised. We cannot say
    why there is <em>redness</em> — why the processing is accompanied by anything at all rather than running in
    the dark, as it manifestly does for the parts of your nervous system managing blood pH. Chalmers called
    this the hard problem in 1995, and it has not moved.</p>
    <p>The live positions, graded honestly:</p>
    <dl class="glossary">
      <dt>Physicalism <span class="spec">◆</span></dt>
      <dd>Consciousness is what certain information processing is; the puzzle is a confusion that will dissolve. Majority view; no demonstration yet.</dd>
      <dt>Global Workspace / Higher-Order theories <span class="spec">◆</span></dt>
      <dd>Experience arises when information is broadcast widely enough to be available to many systems. Testable, productive, contested.</dd>
      <dt>Integrated Information Theory <span class="spec">◆</span></dt>
      <dd>Experience is identical to integrated information (Φ). Mathematically bold, accused by critics of being unfalsifiable and of granting experience to grids of logic gates.</dd>
      <dt>Panpsychism <span class="spec">◆</span></dt>
      <dd>Experience is fundamental, like charge. Avoids the emergence miracle, inherits the combination problem: how do atoms of experience make one unified mind?</dd>
      <dt>Idealism and the Law of One <span class="myth">◆</span></dt>
      <dd>Consciousness is primary and matter is its appearance. A coherent and ancient position, and the one <a href="/">this order's seventh limb</a> engages with — held here as a serious philosophical and esoteric claim, not an empirical result.</dd>
    </dl>
    <p class="muted mt-1">EGregoRA takes no house position. Anyone who tells you this is solved is selling
    something, including when they are selling materialism.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<!-- ============================== PRACTICE ================================ -->
<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">Application</p>
    <h2>What To Actually Do With This</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">Four practices with a defensible mechanism behind them, and nothing to buy.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid three">
    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "spiral" %}</div>
      <h3>Lengthen the Out-Breath</h3>
      <p>Exhaling longer than you inhale raises vagal tone and shifts autonomic balance towards parasympathetic
      within a minute or two. Four in, eight out, five times. The most reliably evidenced intervention on this
      entire page, and it is free.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "tree" %}</div>
      <h3>Go Outside Without a Destination</h3>
      <p>Natural settings restore directed attention and lower measured stress markers; the effect is modest,
      replicated, and multiplied by removing the phone. <a href="/">Limb II</a> has the druidic frame; this is
      the mechanism underneath it.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "star" %}</div>
      <h3>Defend Your Sleep First</h3>
      <p>Before any practice, any supplement, any technique. Chronic short sleep degrades emotional regulation,
      memory consolidation and judgement more thoroughly than almost anything you could add. Visions on four
      hours a night are a symptom.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "eye" %}</div>
      <h3>Watch the Prior, Not the Percept</h3>
      <p>Given Plate IV, the useful contemplative move is not to interrogate what you saw but to notice what you
      were expecting. Most of the content of a strong experience is your own model handed back to you wearing a
      costume.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "seed" %}</div>
      <h3>Keep a Dated Record</h3>
      <p>Write the experience down the same hour, before the mind tidies it into a better story. Memory is
      reconstructive — each recall rewrites the trace. A contemporaneous note is the only honest evidence you
      will ever have about your own inner life.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="frame card reveal">
      <div class="card-glyph">{% glyph "metatron" %}</div>
      <h3>Know the Contraindications</h3>
      <p>A family history of psychosis or bipolar disorder, certain cardiac conditions and several medication
      classes — SSRIs, MAOIs, lithium — change the risk picture of intense practice and of psychedelics
      completely. This is a matter for a clinician, not an order.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

