<!-- ============================== TIMELINE ================================ -->
<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">Lineage</p>
    <h2>How We Learned This</h2>
    <ul class="timeline">
      <li><span class="when">1791</span> Galvani makes a dead frog's leg twitch and establishes that nerves run on electricity.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1848</span> A tamping iron passes through Phineas Gage's frontal lobe; he survives, and personality is shown to be tissue.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1873</span> Golgi's silver stain renders single cells visible; Cajal uses it to prove the brain is discrete neurons, not a continuous web.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1924</span> Berger records the first human EEG and names the alpha rhythm.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1926</span> Klüver catalogues the four form constants in mescaline intoxication.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1943</span> Hofmann's accidental ingestion of LSD-25 opens the serotonergic era.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1953</span> Aserinsky and Kleitman discover REM sleep; dreaming becomes measurable.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1957</span> Patient H.M. loses his hippocampi and reveals that memory is plural and localised.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1963</span> Hodgkin and Huxley take the Nobel for the ionic basis of the action potential.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1971</span> O'Keefe finds place cells — an actual map of space, made of neurons.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1990</span> Ogawa demonstrates the BOLD signal; fMRI makes the living brain watchable.</li>
      <li><span class="when">1995</span> Chalmers formulates the hard problem of consciousness.</li>
      <li><span class="when">2001</span> Raichle describes the default mode network.</li>
      <li><span class="when">2012</span> Carhart-Harris shows psilocybin <em>decreasing</em> brain activity, overturning the expectation of a stimulated brain.</li>
      <li><span class="when">2021</span> AlphaFold-era structural biology begins resolving receptor conformations that were guesswork a decade earlier.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

