<!-- ============================== GLOSSARY ================================ -->
<section class="wrap">
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame reveal">
      <h2>Glossary</h2>
      <dl class="glossary">
        <dt>Action potential</dt>
        <dd>The all-or-nothing electrical spike a neuron fires when its membrane voltage crosses threshold.</dd>
        <dt>Synaptic plasticity</dt>
        <dd>Lasting change in the strength of a connection between two neurons; the substrate of learning.</dd>
        <dt>Entrainment</dt>
        <dd>The pulling of an oscillator's rhythm towards an external periodic drive — drum, flicker, chant.</dd>
        <dt>Predictive processing</dt>
        <dd>The account in which the brain generates a model and the senses supply only correction to it.</dd>
        <dt>Default mode network</dt>
        <dd>Midline structures active at rest, handling self-narrative, memory and mental time travel.</dd>
        <dt>5-HT2A</dt>
        <dd>The serotonin receptor subtype through which every classic psychedelic acts.</dd>
        <dt>Form constant</dt>
        <dd>One of the four universal geometric hallucination classes: lattice, cobweb, tunnel, spiral.</dd>
        <dt>Interoception</dt>
        <dd>Perception of the body's internal state — heartbeat, gut, breath — and a major driver of emotion.</dd>
        <dt>Qualia</dt>
        <dd>The felt character of experience: the redness of red. What the hard problem is about.</dd>
        <dt>Neurogenesis</dt>
        <dd>Birth of new neurons. Abundant in development; in the adult human hippocampus, genuinely disputed.</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>

