<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <h2>A Closing Caution</h2>
    <p>This limb is the one most often used as a weapon, in both directions. Materialists wield it to tell
    people their deepest experiences were "just" chemistry; seekers wield a garbled version of it to dress
    wishes in the vocabulary of science. Both are doing the same disreputable thing — borrowing the authority
    of neuroscience to end an argument early.</p>
    <p>Hold the line instead. The mechanism is astonishing and worth learning properly. The experience is real
    as experience, always, whatever produced it. And the question of what any of it <em>means</em> is not a
    neuroscientific question at all, which is precisely why there are nine other limbs.</p>
    <p class="muted small">Nothing on this page is medical or psychiatric advice. If you are unwell, or
    considering any intense practice while on medication, speak to a clinician rather than to an order.</p>
    <p class="mt-1"><a class="btn" href="/ask-ed/">Put a question to Ed</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
